          "summary": "Full-year results. The SEC accepted this filing eight minutes before the filing that disclosed Amendment No. 1, so it cannot support an early-warning claim.\n\nReviewer scope correction: the summary says the going-concern disclosure is 'breaching the covenant', but the model's Section 6.01 assessment was withheld because its quotation did not verify, so no covenant finding on going concern stands for this report. Section 6.01(a) permits a going-concern exception that arises solely from a potential inability to satisfy a financial maintenance covenant, including the Minimum Core Assets Test. This release does not show whether the auditor's paragraph falls inside that carve-out. The company's later Form 8-K (June 5, 2025) states it would be in breach of the going-concern covenant but for the waiver.\n\nReviewer note on timing: this release itself says the company 'has amended its existing term loan', and the SEC accepted the filing disclosing Amendment No. 1 eight minutes later. The lender response was therefore public with this report. Nothing in this report supports an early-warning claim.",
