          "kind": "Synthetic demonstration source",
          "text": "P1 — interface release and affected revenue\nSynthetic operating evidence, compiled July 13, 2027. HelioForge's identity-platform vendor published its generally available breaking authentication endpoint on June 10, 2027. The supported identity platform is used by customers representing 18% of FluxRail's consolidated fiscal 2026 revenue, counted once across customer groups. The vendor continued to make its published endpoint and migration documentation available to FluxRail. The CFO first received the consolidated failure report at 10:00 a.m. New York time on July 13.\n\nP2 — bridge withdrawal and release status\nThe compatibility bridge described in the June 16 management note passed staging tests. A July 5 production security test subsequently showed that it bypassed a required token-expiry control; FluxRail quarantined the bridge that day and did not offer it as a secure workaround thereafter. The July 12 release register, closed at 5:30 p.m. New York time, records: No compatible production connector has been deployed and no documented secure customer workaround is available. The same status remained open at 9:00 a.m. on July 13. The lender's complete consent and waiver register through July 13 contains no extension or waiver of the interface-remediation deadline.\n\nP3 — continuing service and evidence limits\nThe old authentication endpoint continued operating during the vendor's transition window. FluxRail's incident ledger through July 13 records no production incident preventing a regulated approval workflow for more than four consecutive hours. Customers have not delivered written termination or nonrenewal notices. Subscription fees and terms remain unchanged, and FluxRail retains administrative and export control over the configuration library. No later connector deployment, lender decision, current-quarter debt register, bank balance, or trailing-four-quarter EBITDA bridge is contained in this evidence package.",
