          "kind": "Synthetic demonstration source",
          "text": "P1 — automatically synchronized incident ledger\nSynthetic company-database update synchronized for analyst review at 10:00 a.m. New York time on September 10, 2027. Incident FR-2027-094 prevented completion of regulated approval workflows continuously from 9:00 a.m. to noon on September 7. The affected customer groups represented 7% of FluxRail's fiscal 2026 consolidated revenue, counted once. The responsible chief technology officer's acknowledged escalation at 9:20 a.m. on September 7 states the affected workflows and the 7% revenue exposure. The outage was unplanned and did not fall within an announced maintenance window.\n\nP2 — complete portal and dispatch reconciliation\nThe reporting administrator reconciled the full designated lender-portal receipt log and FluxRail's notice-dispatch register through 10:00 a.m. September 10. Neither contains an initial notice for incident FR-2027-094; the last incident notice in both registers concerns FR-2027-081. The incident-routing configuration still used a greater-than-four-hour duration and 10% affected-revenue threshold on September 7. No written lender default or reporting-cure notice has been delivered for FR-2027-094 as of this review, and no waiver of its notice obligation appears in the signed-instrument register.\n\nP3 — restored service and unresolved cause\nProcessing resumed at noon September 7 with no lost, corrupted, or improperly approved records identified by reconciliation. No customer has delivered a written termination or nonrenewal notice. The engineering team is investigating a possible recurrence of the August queue-lock defect; causal identity is not yet established. The September root-cause report and recurrence tests are still in preparation. FluxRail retains configuration-library ownership, administrative control, and export rights. This update does not contain a new financial covenant calculation or evidence of changed debt, cash, or trailing-four-quarter earnings.",
