          "date": "2027-07-19",
          "status": "effective",
          "summary": "The parties retain the facility economics and strengthen the operational protection for reliable integrations after the July compatibility failure. Earlier delivery and production security validation reduce reliance on an unproven staging bridge.\n\nS1 only: failure to deploy a compatible connector or provide a documented secure workaround for the June 10, 2027 vendor change after the July 12 deadline through the July 19 restoration. Historical noncompliance remains visible; no category-A Event of Default is asserted without the contractual lender notice and cure analysis.\n\nExecuted/effective: 2027-07-20",
          "changes": [
            "S1\n\nFuture vendor changes: 30 to 15 calendar days; independently approved security tests; two-Business-Day exception notice.\n\nBefore: Beginning at closing, the Borrower shall maintain supported production connectors for each identity-management or enterprise-resource-planning platform used by customers representing at least 15% of prior-fiscal-year revenue in aggregate. Within 30 calendar days after a vendor publishes a generally available breaking interface change, the Borrower shall either deploy a compatible connector or provide affected customers a documented, secure workaround. A vendor's withdrawal of access despite the Borrower's timely compliance is excepted. The Borrower shall deliver a quarterly connector-status schedule, first covering March 31, 2027, identifying affected revenue, published changes, remediation dates, and open workarounds.\n\nAfter: Beginning at closing, the Borrower shall maintain supported production connectors for each identity-management or enterprise-resource-planning platform used by customers representing at least 15% of prior-fiscal-year revenue in aggregate. For a generally available breaking interface change published by a vendor on or after July 20, 2027, the Borrower shall, within 15 calendar days after publication, either deploy a compatible connector or provide affected customers a documented, secure workaround. Changes published before July 20, 2027 remain subject to the original 30-calendar-day deadline; this amendment does not reset an elapsed deadline. A workaround counts only after production-equivalent compatibility and security tests are documented and approved by an employee independent of its implementation; staging compatibility alone is insufficient. A vendor's withdrawal of access despite the Borrower's timely compliance is excepted. Within two Business Days after a responsible technology officer learns that a qualifying connector or workaround is unsupported or fails those tests, the Borrower shall notify the Lender with affected revenue, the known defect and a remediation plan. The Borrower shall continue to deliver the quarterly connector-status schedule, first covering March 31, 2027, identifying affected revenue, published changes, remediation dates, open workarounds and the required validation records. Failure of the connector and remediation duties retains resolution category A; a missed notice or schedule uses resolution category R."
          ]
