          "summary": "Quarterly results three months before covenant noncompliance was disclosed.\n\nReviewer scope correction: the 'compliant' liquidity finding uses the company's 'Total Available Liquidity' ($97.4 million), which the release defines as unrestricted cash plus availability under floorplan credit facilities. The agreement defines Liquidity as unrestricted cash and Cash Equivalents only. The release gives 'Cash and Restricted Cash' of $61.8 million without separating the unrestricted portion, and no Compliance Certificate is public, so the finding is indicative rather than established.\n\nReviewer note on the weakened leverage assumption: it rests on the company's public Adjusted EBITDA, which is not contractual Consolidated EBITDA. It is a directional signal, not a leverage calculation. This report became public on May 10, 2023; the company disclosed June 30 leverage noncompliance and Amendment No. 5 on August 9, 2023. Nemotron may know RumbleOn's later history from pretraining, so this ordering shows the mechanism and is not proof of early warning.",
